  era: "Section 36 \xB7 Indian Economy Through History \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Ancient trade
  text: Harappans traded with Mesopotamia; later India traded with Persia, Greece, Rome, China and South-East Asia, exporting spices, textiles, gems and ivory. The Roman writer Pliny complained of Roman gold flowing to India.
